  "problem": "A rate, count, percentage and monetary total could share a unit merely because labels look similar. Maternal and infant mortality, crude and adjusted rates, and overlapping ACS estimates could be treated as equivalent. Missing definitions could be invented. An executable API with an unknown measurement denominator could still receive a research-ready badge. Cross-drug, cross-year or cross-population conversions could be inferred without evidence. Editing sealed identity use-card schema or normalization src would break WP7/normalization artifact seals.",
  "resulting_behavior": "Measure semantics live in packages/enrichment/measure-semantics.mjs. Numerator, denominator/universe, scale/unit, adjustment, weight, CI/MOE, suppression and missingness are separately evidenced. A rate, count, percentage and monetary total cannot share a unit merely because labels look similar. Maternal versus infant mortality, crude versus adjusted rates and overlapping ACS estimates are explicit non-equivalences. Optional unknowns are preserved. A research-ready badge is blocked when an essential denominator or unit is missing, including when an API is executable. No cross-drug, cross-year or cross-population conversion is inferred without evidence. Scientific cautions are specific to the selected measure. Sealed packages/identity/schemas/researcher-use-card.schema.json and packages/normalization/src are unchanged.",
